.Dd April 14, 2026
.Dt NOD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nod
.Nd suckless notification daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a minimal notification daemon for X11 that implements enough of the
Desktop Notifications Specification 1.2 over D-Bus to work with
.Xr notify-send 1
and any application that emits standard notifications.
.Pp
.Nm
claims the well-known name
.Pa org.freedesktop.Notifications
on the session bus and displays notifications as override-redirect
X11 windows rendered with Xft.
Only one notification daemon can own that name at a time.
.Pp
Configuration is compile-time only: edit
.Pa config.h
and rebuild.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v
Print version and exit.
.El
.Sh INTERACTION
.Bl -tag -width "Left-click "
.It Sy Left-click
Invoke the
.Dq default
action if the notification registered one, then dismiss.
.It Sy Right-click
Dismiss only. Never invoke action.
.It Sy Timeout
Auto-dismiss after the notification's expire time.
.El
.Sh SUPPORTED HINTS
.Bl -tag -width "urgency (byte)  "
.It Sy urgency No (byte)
0 = low, 1 = normal, 2 = critical.
Selects colors and default timeout from
.Pa config.h .
.El
.Pp
All other hints are ignored.
HTML/pango markup in
.Sy summary
and
.Sy body
is stripped; only plain text is rendered.
.Sh CAPABILITIES
.Nm
advertises
.Sy body
and
.Sy actions
via
.Sy GetCapabilities .
It does not advertise
.Sy body-markup ,
.Sy body-images ,
.Sy icon-static ,
.Sy persistence ,
or
.Sy sound .
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width "SIGUSR1 "
.It Sy SIGINT , SIGTERM
Clean up windows, release the D-Bus name, exit.
.It Sy SIGUSR1
Reload colors and font from X resources.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "config.def.h "
.It Pa config.h
Per-user appearance, timeouts, position, stacking, and corner radius.
Copied from
.Pa config.def.h
on first build.
Rounded corners use the X Shape extension when available.
.El
.Sh X RESOURCES
When
.Sy use_xresources
is enabled in
.Pa config.h ,
.Nm
reads the following resources at startup.
Unset resources fall back to the compiled-in defaults from
.Pa config.h .
.Bl -tag -width "nod.background.critical "
.It Sy nod.font
Font pattern passed to Xft, e.g.\& Li monospace:size=10 .
.It Sy nod.background.low
.It Sy nod.background.normal
.It Sy nod.background.critical
Background color per urgency.
.It Sy nod.foreground.low
.It Sy nod.foreground.normal
.It Sy nod.foreground.critical
Foreground color per urgency.
.It Sy nod.border.low
.It Sy nod.border.normal
.It Sy nod.border.critical
Border color per urgency.
.El
.Pp
When
.Sy use_xresources
is enabled, nod polls the X resource database every
.Sy xresources_poll_ms
milliseconds and reloads colors and font automatically.
Set
.Sy xresources_poll_ms
to 0 to disable polling; send
.Sy SIGUSR1
to force a reload.
.Pp
Example
.Pa ~/.Xresources :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nod.font:              Noto Sans:size=10
nod.background.normal: #1d2021
nod.foreground.normal: #ebdbb2
nod.border.normal:     #458588
nod.border.critical:   #cc241d
.Ed
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start from
.Pa ~/.xinitrc
before the window manager:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nod &
exec dwm
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nod-send 1 ,
.Xr notify-send 1 ,
.Xr gdbus 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Matteo Merola
.Sh BUGS
Only one default action is respected;
other action keys are ignored.
No icon, sound, or markup support by design.
